; Leg DE -- the host SENDS.  The Victor RECEIVES with --rtscts at the
; SHIPPING water marks.
;
; THE LEG THAT LICENSES THE DEFAULT.  DB proves the mechanism reaches the
; far end; this proves that turning it on changes nothing when it is not
; needed, which is the actual shipping configuration.  Only run it if DB
; passed.
;
; PASS:  held=0 rel=0 -- the 3,072 mark is above every occupancy this port
;        has recorded (rxpeak 2,581, SS16af) -- byte-exact, rxlost=0
;        rxfull=0, and the whole leg indistinguishable from DN.
;
; A held>0 here would be interesting rather than wrong: it would mean this
; cable or this sitting drives the ring deeper than any before it, and the
; rxpeak on DN is the number to read it against.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set retry 30
set parity none
set flow rts/cts
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16ajDE.pkt
send rcvde.dat
statistics
